    "created_at": "2016-10-15T16:53:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-15T16:54:35Z",
    "body": "This should be fairly clear form the normative description of how to determine an element's directionality. The sentence you quote is just a non-normative summary (that's why it's in the green box). We generally don't detail all the possibilities in the non-normative summary; it's a guide for authors as to what happens if they don't do something weird, not a description of the actual algorithm.\n\nIn any case, it sounds like there's just a bad test. The normative part of the spec is not \"an implication\"; it's the only part that actually matters, for testing behavior.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
